\tag{ftip}
\tag{instruction-tuning}
\tag{provenance}

\card{Remark}{Demonstration and teacher provenance}{
\p{The provenance field #{\omega} distinguishes a demonstration
from the process that supplied it. Ouyang et al. collect labeler-written
demonstrations in \citet{§§3.2, 3.4}{ouyang2022training}. Wei et al. permit a
broader task mixture in \citet{§2; Fig. 2}{wei2022finetuned}.}

\p{Human writers, stronger teacher models, filtered self-generations, and
programmatically produced targets give different information to the learner.
Claims about sample efficiency or capability acquisition must therefore state
which producer and selection rule were available.}
}
